msgid "Boards and lists"
msgstr ""

msgid "The boards overview"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The boards overview is the first screen after signing in. Click "
"**KanbanMF** in the top bar to come back to it from anywhere."
msgstr ""

msgid "The boards overview."
msgstr ""

msgid "Boards are grouped in sections:"
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Starred`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The boards you starred, for quick access. A starred board appears both "
"here and in its own section."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`My Boards`"
msgstr ""

msgid "The boards you created."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Shared with me`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Boards other people created and shared with you. The round avatar on each"
" tile shows its owner."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Templates`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Starting points for new boards — see :doc:`templates`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Click a section's title to fold it away; KanbanMF remembers which "
"sections you folded, in this browser. At the bottom of the page, "
":guilabel:`Show Archived Boards` lists the boards you archived and "
":guilabel:`Show Overdue Tasks` opens the :doc:`overdue tasks <overdue>` "
"page."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The order, the stars and the colours are **yours alone**: someone you "
"share a board with can star it, colour it and place it differently on "
"their own overview without affecting yours."
msgstr ""

msgid "Creating a board"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Click :guilabel:`Create a new Board`, type its name and click **Save**. "
"Tick :guilabel:`Starred` to star it straight away."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The dialog to create a board, with a template chosen and the lists\n"
"it will create."
msgstr ""

msgid "Creating a board from a template."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you have templates, or someone shared one with you, the dialog also "
"offers a :guilabel:`Template`. Choose one to start the board with a copy "
"of its lists — the dialog previews them. Leave it on :guilabel:`None "
"(empty board)` for a board with no lists."
msgstr ""

msgid "Starring and reordering"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Click the star on a board's tile to star it, and again to unstar it. To "
"change the order of the boards in a section, drag a tile by its four-"
"arrow handle and drop it where you want it."
msgstr ""

msgid "The board menu on the overview"
msgstr ""

msgid "Each tile has a menu (☰) at its top right."
msgstr ""

msgid "A board tile with its menu open."
msgstr ""

msgid "The menu of a board you own."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Change Name`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Rename the board. Owner only."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Change Color`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Pick the board's colour, or :guilabel:`Reset to default`. The colour "
"tints the tile and the board itself, and is only what *you* see."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Share`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Share the board with other people — see :doc:`sharing`. Owner only."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`E-Mail notification`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Your due-date reminders for this board — see :doc:`notifications`."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Archive Board`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Owner only; see below."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On a board shared with you, the menu only has the items you can use: the "
"colour and your e-mail notifications."
msgstr ""

msgid "Archiving and deleting a board"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Archiving hides a board from the overview — for you and for everyone it "
"is shared with — without losing anything. To see your archived boards, "
"click :guilabel:`Show Archived Boards` at the bottom of the overview."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Archived Boards section with one board."
msgstr ""

msgid "An archived board."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each archived board's menu has :guilabel:`Restore Board`, which puts it "
"back where it was, and :guilabel:`Delete Board`, which deletes it "
"permanently, with its lists and cards. Deleting can't be undone, and a "
"board can only be deleted once it is archived."
msgstr ""

msgid "Working on a board"
msgstr ""

msgid "Click a board's tile to open it."
msgstr ""

msgid "A board with four lists."
msgstr ""

msgid "A board."
msgstr ""

msgid "The bar under the board's name holds:"
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Add List`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Add a new list at the right end of the board."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Labels`"
msgstr ""

msgid "The board's labels — see :ref:`manual-labels`."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Sort cards`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"How the cards are ordered in every list of the board — see :ref:`manual-"
"sorting`."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Archive`"
msgstr ""

msgid "The board's archived lists and cards — see :ref:`manual-archive`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The menu (☰) at the right of the bar has your :guilabel:`E-Mail "
"notification` settings for the board."
msgstr ""

msgid "Lists"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each list's header has three controls: the four-arrow handle to drag the "
"list to another position, **+** to add a card to it (see :doc:`cards`), "
"and the list menu (☰)."
msgstr ""

msgid "A list with its menu open."
msgstr ""

msgid "The list menu."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Archive All Cards`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Archive every card in the list in one go — handy for clearing out a "
"*Done* list. The list itself stays."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Rename List`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Change the list's name."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The list's colour, again only for you. New cards you add to a coloured "
"list take its colour."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Archive List`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hide the list, with all its cards, from the board."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Everyone with access to the board can add, rename, reorder and archive "
"lists."
msgstr ""

msgid "Sorting cards"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Sort cards menu."
msgstr ""

msgid "The sort options."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Custom order`"
msgstr ""

msgid "The order you arrange by dragging cards. This is the default."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Due date`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Cards with no due date first — still in the order you dragged them into —"
" then the dated ones, soonest first. Only the undated cards can be moved "
"by hand; a dated card's place follows from its date."
msgstr ""

msgid ":guilabel:`Alphabetically (A-Z)` and :guilabel:`Alphabetically (Z-A)`"
msgstr ""

msgid "By card name."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The choice applies to every list of the board, and is remembered per "
"board, in this browser."
msgstr ""

msgid "Archived lists and cards"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":guilabel:`Archive` in the board's bar shows what has been archived on "
"the board: archived lists, with their cards, and archived cards from "
"lists that are still on the board."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Archived Lists & Cards view."
msgstr ""

msgid "Archived lists and cards."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use a list's or a card's menu (☰) to :guilabel:`Restore` it to the board."
" The board's owner can also delete it permanently from the same menu; "
"that can't be undone. :guilabel:`Return to Board` takes you back."
msgstr ""

